  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "Description of Our Services",
    "text": "Description of Our Services: We are not a lender or fiduciary. For the CAB fee set forth below, we will attempt to (1) obtain a loan in the amount and for the term set forth below from DSI Lending Resources, Inc., a third party lender, with a contract rate of interest of no more than ten percent per annum (10%); (2) issue a letter of credit (“LOC”) to secure that loan; and (3) assist you in preparing and completing documents necessary to obtain the loan. The estimated period for performing these services shall be one day, Additionally, we will also attempt to: (4) assist you in creating a positive credit history, if requested, through routine reporting of your payments to an allernative consumer reporting agency; (5) assist you in making your payments timely by providing a reminder service; (6) upon request, provide consumer financial cducation materials; (7) where available, provide discounted check cashing services to facilitate payment(s); and (8) maintain a network of branch locations to provide certain CAB services. These additional services may be provided throughout the term, We do not promise that you will actually receive a loan. All credit decisions shall be made by a third party lender. HOWEVER, YOU WILL NOT OWE US A FEE IP YOUR LOAN APPLICATION IS DENIED BY THE LENDER, The precise amount of your finance charge will depend upon the amount that the lender allows you to borrow, and the term of the loan. You have been advised that our CAB services and the third party loan, if any, you receive may not be at the lowest rate or vest terms available, and that you may look elsewhere for credit services and a loan. A credit access business must comply with Chapter 392 and the federal Fair Debt Collection Practices Act (15 U.S.C. Section 1692 et seq.) with respect to an extension of consumer credit described by Section 393.602(a). A credit access business must comply, to the extent applicable, with 10 U.S.C. Section 987 and any regulations adopted under that law with respect to an cxtension of consumer eredit described by Section 393.602(a)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "Disclosure of Fee as Finance Charge",
    "text": "Disclosure of Fee as Finance Charge: Although the fee that we charge you is not interest, the Federal Trath in Lending Act requires that it be included in the finance charge calculation for your loan."
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "Cost and Payment Terms",
    "text": "COST AND PAYMENT TERMS. Our CAB fee is based upon 708.90% annualized rate on the amount finaneed on the loan to you by the Lender, Our CAB fee is due when the loan is made and is financed as part of the loan to you from the Lender, On the payday installment loan of $300.00 you have applied for, payable in LO payments with interest of 10.00% per annum charged by the Lender, the Amount Financed is 300,00, the Pinance Charge is $561.15. The Finanee Charge consists of the interest paid or to be paid to the Lender, in the amount of $3.00 and our CAB fee for this transaction of $556.15. ‘The Annual Percentage Rate is 713.38%, payments commencing on 4/20/2012, in the amount of $86.15, Followed by regular bi-weekly payments of $86.15 each, with a final payment of $85.80 on 8/24/2012, and the Total of Payments is $86.15. You will be entitled to a refund of part of the CAB fee based on a prorated daily basis for the final period with respect to payment in full or acceleration of maturity. Under any loan that we may abtain for you, if you pay off your loan early, you will not have to pay a penalty and your finance charge may be reduced. There is no prepayment penalty,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "Other Fees and Reimbursement",
    "text": "Besides the CAB fees, you are responsible to reimburse CAB for any amounts CAB pays the Lender on the letter of credit, plus 10% per annum until (he reimbursement is paid, a return item fee of $30 for any check, ACH debit, electronic check, or other payment device that is returned unpaid, attorneys’ fees, and costs of collection, Besides interest to the Lender, you would be responsible to the Lender for a late charge equal to the greater of 5% or $7.50, if payment is 10 or more days late, a return item {ce of $30 for any check, ACH debit, electronic check, or other payment device that is returned unpaid, and attorneys! fees, and costs of collection,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "LOC and Obligation to Reimburse",
    "text": "juest us to issue our irrevocable LOC in favor of the third party lender as beneficiary in accordance with LOC and Obligation to Reimburse: You rec licable, on Chapter $ of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, in an amount not to exceed principal, interest, returned item fee, and late fee, as app the loan that we arrange for you. You agree fo pay us any amounts paid by us to third parties pursuant to the LOC. Our payment on the LOC to the lender is conditioned upon presentnent by the lender to us of(a) the lender's sight draft, and (b) the lender's statement that your loan is in default and hag been in default at least 10 days from its due date. The LOC will expire the earlier of 55 days after maturity of the loan we arrange for you or the date the loan is paid in full, If you timely exercise your right to cancel this Agreement, our LOC shall be automatically revoked and shal! have no further effect. You instruct us to pay the lender’s sight draft up to the maximum amount of the LOC upon presentation to us of documentation complying with the conditions set forth above. You understand that we are nol responsible for determining the accuracy of any statement made by the lender/ LOC beneficiary and that our duty is strictly to pay upon proper presentment of documents. No part of this Agreement, nor any charge or receipt by us, is intended to permit us to Impose any amount in excess of lawful amounts. If an unlawful excess occurs, we will apply if as a credit or otherwise refund if and (he rate or amount involved will automatically be reduced to the maximum lawful rate or amount, To the extent permitted by law, for purposes of determining our compliance with law, we may calculate charges by amortizing, prorating, allocating or spreading."
  },
