  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "Waiver of Jury Trial and Arbitration Provision — Introduction",
    "text": "WAIVER OF JURY TRIAL AND ARBITRATION PROVISION: Arbitration is a process in which persons with a dispute: (a) waive their rights to file a lawsuit and proceed in court and to have a jury vial to resolve their disputes; and (b) agrec, instead, to submit their disputes to a neutral third person (an “arbitrator”) for a decision. Each party to the dispute has an opportunity to present some evidence to the arbitrator, Pre-arbitration discovery may be limited. Arbitration proceedings are private and less formal than court trials. The arbitrator will issue a final and binding decision resolving the dispute, which may be enforced as a court judgment, A court rarcly overturns an arbitrator’s decision. THEREFORE, YOU ACKNOWLEDGE AND AGREE AS FOLLOWS:"
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "Paragraph 1 — Definition of \"dispute\" (Waiver of Jury Trial and Arbitration Provision)",
    "text": "1. For purposes of this Waiver of Jury Trial and Arbitration Provision (hercinafler the “Arbitration Provision”), the words “dispute” and “disputes” are given the broadest possible meaning and include, without limitation (a) all claims, disputes, or controversies arising from or relating directly or indirectly to the signing of this Arbitration Provision, Ue validity and scope of this Arbitration Provision and any claim or attempt to set aside this Arbitration Provision; (b) all federal or state law claims, disputes or controversics, arising from or relating directly or indirectly to this Agreement(including the Arbilration Provision), the information you gave us before entering into this Disclosure Statement, and/or any past and/or future claims or disputes between you and us and/or any Lender who provides you with a loan as a result of our services (the “Lender”), (c) all counterclaims, cross-claims and third party claims; (d) all common law claims, based upon contract, tort, fraud, or other intentional torts; (¢) all claims based upon a violation of any state or federal constitution, statule or regulation; (f) all claims asserted by us against you, including claims for money damages to collect any sum we claim you owe us and/or the Lender; (g) all claims asserted by you individually against us and/or any of our employees, agents, directors, officers, shareholders, managers, members, parent Company or affiliated entities (hereinaNer collectively referred to as “related third parties”), including claims for money damages and/or equitable or injunctive relief; (h) all claims asserted on your behalf by another person, (1) all claims asserted by you as a private attorney general, as a representative and member of a class of persons, or in any ather representative capacity, against us and/or related third parties (hereinafter reterred to as “Representative Claims\"); and/or (j) all claims arising from or relating directly or indirectly to the disclosure by us or related third partics of any non-public personal information about you,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "Arbitration 2(a) Waiver of jury trial",
    "text": "2. You acknowledge and agree that by cntepi-a into this Arbitration Provision: poy, (a) YOU ARE GIVING UP YOUR RIC¢ TO HAVE A TRIAL BY JURY TO RESOLV — VY DISPUTE ALLEGED AGAINST US, THE LENDER AND/OR OUR/ITS = RELATED THIRD PARTIES;"
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "Arbitration 2(b) Waiver of court",
    "text": "(vp) YOU ARE GIVING UP YOUR RIGHT TO HAVE A COURT, OTHER THAN A SMALL CLAIMS TRIBUNAL, RESOLVE ANY DISPUTE ALLEGED AGAINST — US, THE LENDER AND/OR OURATS RELATED THIRD PARTIES; and"
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "Arbitration 2(c) Waiver of representative capacity",
    "text": "(c) YOU ARE GIVING UP YOUR RIGHT TO SERVE AS A REPRESENTATIVE, AS A PRIVATE ATTORNEY GENERAL, OR IN ANY OTHER REPRESENTATIVE CAPACITY, OR TO PARTICIPATE AS A MEMBER OF A CLASS OF CLAIMANTS, IN ANY LAWSUIT FILED AGAINST US, THE LENDER AND/OR OUR/AITS RELATED THIRD PARTIES. YOUR DISPUTE MAY NOT BE CONSOLIDATED WITH THE DISPUTE OF ANY OTHER PERSON(S) FOR ANY PURPOSE(S),"
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "Arbitration 3. Individual basis only",
    "text": "3. Except as provided in Paragraph 6 below, all disputes including any Representative Claims against us, the Lender and/or our/its related third parties shall be resolved by binding arbitration only on an individual basis with you. THEREFORE, THE ARBITRATOR SHALL NOT CONDUCT CLASS ARBITRATION; THAT IS, THE ARBITRATOR SHALL NOT ALLOW YOU TO SERVE AS A REPRESENTATIVE, AS A PRIVATE ATTORNEY GENERAL, OR IN ANY OTHER REPRESENTATIVE CAPACITY FOR OTHERS IN THE ARBITRATION. Notwithstanding any other provision herein to the contrary, the validity, effect, and enforceability of this waiver of class action lawsuit and class-wide arbitration shall be determined solely by a court of competent jurisdiction and not by the arbitrator. If the arbitrator fails or refuses to abide by the class-wide arbitration waiver and the court refuses to enforce the class-wide arbitration waiver, the parties agree that the dispute will proceed in court under applicable court rules and procedures, following all appeals, if any, of the court's decision."
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "Arbitration 4. Election and selection of arbitration organization",
    "text": "4, Upon the election by you, us, or Lender, any dispute shall be resolved by binding arbitration in accordance with this arbitration provision and the rules of the arbitration organization that is sclected. Either you, we, or Lender, as applicable, may give written notice to the other of an intention to require arbitration of the other party's dispute at any time, even if the other party has begun a lawsuit. If a judgment has been entered in a lawsuit regarding a dispute, however, then neither we, Lender, nor you ean demand arbitration on the matters included in the judgment. Affer notice by either party to the other, you may select the arbitration organization of your choice from: American Arbitration Association, 335 Madison Avenue, New York, NY 10017, www.adr.org, (800) 778-7879; JAMS 1920 Main Street, Suite 300, Irvine, CA 92614, jamsadr.com, 800-352-5267; or any other arbitrator (including an attamey, retired judge, or an arbitrator registered and in good standing with an arbitration association) reasonably satisfactory to us. [f you do not select an arbitrator within 20 days after notice, we shall be entitled to select one. If the named organization will not conduct the arbitration according to this provision, or if we are not able to agree on another arbitrator, you agree that we may ask any court of competent jurisdiction to appoint an arbitrator to conduct the arbitration in accordance with this arbitration agreement. ‘The individual arbitrator shall be chosen in accordance with the rules of the selected arbitration organization, but if that organization or arbitrator has no published rules, then in accordance with the Rules of the AAA for Consumer Arbitrations, You, we, and Lender agree that any arbitration organization that permits class actions in arbitration may not be selected to arbitrate disputes, If you ask us fo, we or Lender, as applicable, will advance all or part of the arbitration filing, administrative, and/or hearing fees required for the arbitration, up to $1000; the arbitrator will decide whether we, Lender, or you, as applicable, will ultimately be responsible to pay those fees. In no event will you be required to reimburse us or Lender for any arbitration filing, administrative and/or hearing fees in an amount greater than what your court costs would have been if the dispute had been resolved in a state court with jurisdiction. IC is the intention of CAB and Lender to comply with applicable law, In cach and every instance, CAB’s and Lender's respective rights are limited by applicable law (to the extent they may not be lawfully waived), construed so as to comply with applicable laws, and CAB’s and Lender's rights may not be exercised except to the extent permitted by applicable law. No charge or receipt by CAB or Lender, or any other person on CAB’s or Lender's behalf, is intended to exceed lawful amounts. I an unlawful excess occurs, it will be applied as a credit or otherwise refunded, and the rate or amount involved will automatically be rcduced to the maximum lawful rate or amount. fo the extent permitted by law, for purposes of determining CAB’s and Lender's compliance with the law, CAI and Lender may calculate charges by amortizing, prorating, allocating and spreading. Rach party agrees to provide the other written notice and a reasonable opportunity of at least 30 days to remedy any circumstances that the parly contends might preclude arbitration of a dispute."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "Arbitration 5. Arbitration fees and procedure",
    "text": "5. Regardless of who demands arbitration, at your request we will advance your portion of the arbitration expenses, including the Dling, administrative, hearing and arbitrator's fees (“Arbitration Fees”). ‘Throughout the arbitration, each party shall bear his or her own altorncys’ feces and expenses, such as witness and expert witness fees; but without limitation of any party’s ability to recover costs and attorneys’ fees (o the extent authorized by law. The arbitrator shall apply applicable substantive law consistent with the Federal Arbitration Act (“PAA”), and applicable statutes of limitation, and shall honor claims of privilege recognized at law. ‘The arbitration hearing will be conducted in the county of your residence, or within 30 miles from such county, or in such other place as shall be ordered by the arbitrator. The arbitrator may decide, with or without a hearing, any motion that is substantially similar fo a motion to dismiss for failure to state a claim or a motion for summary judgment. In conducting the arbitration proceeding, the arbitrator shall not apply any federal or state rules of civil procedure or evidence, If the arbitrator renders a decision or an award in your favor resolving the dispute, then you will not be responsible for reimbursing us for your portion of the Arbitration Fees, and we will reimburse you for any Arbitration Fees you have previously paid. If the arbitrator does not render a decision or an award in your favor resolving the dispute, then the arbitrator shall require you to reimburse us for the Arbitration Fees we have advanced, not to exceed the amount which would have been assessed as court cosis if the dispute had been resolved by a state court with jurisdiction, less any Arbitration Fees you have previously paid. At the timely request of any party, the arbitrator shall provide a written explanation for the award. The arbitrator's award may be fled with any court having jurisdiction."
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "Arbitration 6. Small claims tribunal",
    "text": "6. All parties, including related third parties, shall retain the right to seek adjudication in a small claims tribunal for disputes within the scope of such tribunal’s jurisdiction, Any dispute, which cannot be adjudicated within the jurisdiction of a small claims tribunal, shall be resolved by binding arbitration. Any appeal of a judgment from a small claims tribunal shall be resolved by binding arbitration."
  },
  {
    "id": "c025",
    "name": "Arbitration 7. Governing law of arbitration provision",
    "text": "7. This Arbitration Provision is made pursuant to a transaction involving interstate commerce and shall be governed by the FAA, Uf a final, non-appealable judgment of a court having jurisdiction over this ransaction finds, for any reason, thal the FAA does not apply to this transaction, then our agreement to arbitrate shall be governed by the arbitration law of the State of Texas."
  },
  {
    "id": "c026",
    "name": "Arbitration 8. Binding effect and severability",
    "text": "8. This Arbitration Provision is binding upon and benefits you, your respective heirs, successors and assigns, This Arbitration Provision is binding upon and benefits us, the Lender, and/or our/its successors and assigns, and related third parties. This Arbitration Provision continues in fill force and effect, even if your obligations have been paid or discharged (rough bankruptcy. This Arbitration Provision survives any (ermination, amendment, expiration or performance of any transaction between you and us and continues in full foree and effect unless you and we otherwise agree in writing. 1f any of this Arbitration Provision is held invalid, (he remainder shall remain in effect, unless the provision precluding the arbitrator from conducting a class or consolidated arbitration as set forth in paragraph 3 above is deemed invalid or unenforceable, in which case this entire Arbitration Provision shall be decmed void and the partics shall proceed in court,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c027",
    "name": "Arbitration 9. Opt-Out Process",
    "text": "OPT-OUT PROCESS. You may choose, f fo opt-out of and not be subject to this Arbitration Provision but only by following the process set forth below. If you do nol wish to be subject to“ “Arbitration Provision, then you must notify us inf” “ng within nincty (90) calendar days of the date of this Agreement at (he following address PL. Juan Store of Texas, Inc., Attn: Arbitration Opt-Ou, . 8 Loan Store of Texas, Inc., 300 North Elizabeth, 4th Floor, Chicago, 1. 60607. Your written notice must include your name, address, social securily number, the date of this Agreement, and a statement that you wish to opt-out of this Arbitration Provision. Your notice to opt-out will only apply to this particular (ransaction with us and not to subsequent or previous transactions, a separate opt-out notice is required for each transaction on which you wish to opt-out of this Arbitration Provision."
  },
  {
